** I will be adding game concepts here**

Game Objectives:

- Collect three distinct items, each belonging to either Julian, Ricky, or Bubbles, and successfully deliver each item without getting caught by Randy.
- The player starts with three lives at the beginning of the game, and may lose a life if they run into Randy (similar to Pacman).
- The player must interact with a character to enable their specific item quest.
- All quests may be active at the same time.
- Randy will stand guard around a grill, making it impossible to get to and steal the grill (for the cookout as per the story)
- Once the player successfully returns all three items to each trailer park boy, the boys will distract Randy for a period of time, 
  drawing his attention away from the grill, allowing our player to get their hands on it, thus winning the game.

Randy:

- The player may alert Randy if they approach too closely causing him to chase the player at the same speed as the player.
- Randy will not cease chasing the player until the player runs into a "dirty burger" (a finite number may be placed around the map and are only visible 
  when the player is being chased).
- When the player runs into a "dirty burger", Randy is calmed and returns to the grill. 
- If Randy catches the player, Randy’s portrait appears with specific dialogue indicating the player’s status.
- If the player still has a game life after getting caught, a portrait of Randy will appear alongside a specific dialogue (strikes one and two).
- If the player is out of game lives, Randy’s portrait appears with a different dialogue, and the player is placed under trailer arrest, ending the game.

Items:

- There are three retrievable items including a bag of ice cubes (for Julian), a pack of chicken fingers (for Ricky), and a lost Kitty (for Bubbles). 
- Each item may be stored within different objects at random, with the default locations for each being the ice chest for the bag of ice, 
  the big oak tree for the kitty, and trailer for the chicken fingers (maybe we only randomize the the location for the chicken fingers, 
  with the ice cubes and the kitty always being located in the ice chest and oak tree for simplicity).
- Each location could appear on the map as default map objects, with other trailers being placed as obstacles around the map. 
- The player may only carry one object at a time for difficulty’s sake, and upon trying to pick up a second item, the player will receive a message 
  (for example, “Your pockets are full, and may only carry one item at a time”.)



